## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design a CKNE-aware ingestion control loop that dynamically adapts per-tenant throughput while ensuring SLA guarantees and system stability under CKNE shifts.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-priority mapping: P = 1 + ckne (higher CKNE → higher priority)
- CKNE-to-batch window mapping: W = baseW * (1 - ckne/2) (higher CKNE → smaller batches, faster processing)
- Exponential backoff: delay = baseDelay * 2^retryCount for retries
- Minute-by-minute scheduler: reweights quota allocation each cycle based on current CKNE
- SLA preservation: baseline minimum quota guaranteed even for ckne=0 tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
function quotaForTenant(ckne, baseBatchWindowMs, basePriority) {
  const priority = basePriority + ckne;
  const batchWindow = baseBatchWindowMs * (1 - ckne / 2);
  return { priority, batchWindow };
}

// Example: tenant A with ckne=0.65
quotaForTenant(0.65, 60000, 1); 
// → { priority: 1.65, batchWindow: 31500ms }
```
